<section>
  <grid spacing="medium">
    <grid-item colspan="22" padding="24pt" vertical-align="end" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.18">
      <ai-image background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="portrait" prompt="Layered cut-paper museum-table illustration of an opened folded map reconnected to a tax paper, a tied letter and a food basket by one winding postcard-red paper thread, warm cream ground, river-blue geography marks and sun-yellow discovery tabs, clear daylight, no people, no flags, no weapons, no readable text"/>
      <labels><label variant="solid">Illustrated reconstruction</label></labels>
      <h3>The objects reconnect</h3>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="38">
      <h2>What changed—and what did not?</h2>
      <grid direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" spacing="small">
        <grid-item cell-style="subtle">
          <labels><label variant="solid">Changed</label></labels>
          <h3>The conflict stopped</h3>
          <p>The ten-year conflict ended in 1845.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item cell-style="subtle">
          <labels><label variant="outline">Did not change</label></labels>
          <ul>
            <li>Rio Grande do Sul did not remain separate from Brazil.</li>
            <li>Abolition was not an outcome of the revolt; slavery continued.</li>
          </ul>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug">
        <grid-item background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt">
          <h4>Big idea</h4>
          <p>Ending a conflict does not automatically make life fair for everyone.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>